{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10596","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:57:09.904336+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"This is a rather niche use case of `do_bench_cudagraph`. You're recommended to warm up the kernel first","created_at":"2026-06-13T12:01:11Z","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/10596#issuecomment-4698456896","id":4698456896,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10596","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABGAzDQA","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/4698456896/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-06-13T12:01:11Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/4698456896","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2306281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jokeren","id":2306281,"login":"Jokeren","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDYyODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Describe the bug\n\nThe do_bench/_cudagraph function did not consider if it executed during cuda graph capturing, so when an auto tune is triggered under cuda graph capture, the sync call inside the do_bench/_cudagraph function will invalidate the stream and cause the capturing to fail.\n\nTo reproduce, just run an uncached auto tune kernel during Cuda Graph Capture. I do not know if this is valid use case, but I guess it is(?), anyway, just let you know.\n\n```Python\n\"\"\"Vector Addition from triton tutorial, removed most of the comment for clarity\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\nDEVICE = triton.runtime.driver.active.get_active_torch_device()\n\n\n# add a dead simple autotune config\n@triton.autotune(\n    configs=[\n        triton.Config({\"BLOCK_SIZE\": 64}, num_warps=2),\n        triton.Config({\"BLOCK_SIZE\": 128}, num_warps=4),\n    ],\n    key=[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"],\n    do_bench=triton.testing.do_bench_cudagraph\n)\n@triton.jit\ndef add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, output_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n    block_start = pid * BLOCK_SIZE\n    offsets = block_start + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    mask = offsets < n_elements\n    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n    output = x + y\n    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, output, mask=mask)\n\n\ndef add(x: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor):\n    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n    assert x.device == DEVICE and y.device == DEVICE and output.device == DEVICE\n    n_elements = output.numel()\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"]),)\n    # remove fixed BLOCK_SIZE\n    add_kernel[grid](x, y, output, n_elements)\n    return output\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    torch.manual_seed(0)\n    size = 98432\n    x = torch.rand(size, device=DEVICE)\n    y = torch.rand(size, device=DEVICE)\n\n    # use it with cuda graph before any cache exists\n    # the sync call inside do_bench_cudagraph will invalidate the cuda graph capture\n    with torch.cuda.stream(torch.cuda.Stream()):\n        g = torch.cuda.CUDAGraph()\n        with torch.cuda.graph(g):\n            add(x, y)\n        torch.cuda.synchronize()\n\n        g.replay()\n        torch.cuda.synchronize()\n```\n\nFailed with the following error:\n\n```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/triton-cuda-graph-auto-tune.py\", line 53, in <module>\n    add(x, y)\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/triton-cuda-graph-auto-tune.py\", line 38, in add\n    add_kernel[grid](x, y, output, n_elements)\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/runtime/jit.py\", line 370, in <lambda>\n    return lambda *args, **kwargs: self.run(grid=grid, warmup=False, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/runtime/autotuner.py\", line 240, in run\n    benchmark()\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/runtime/autotuner.py\", line 229, in benchmark\n    timings = {config: self._bench(*args, config=config, **kwargs) for config in pruned_configs}\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/runtime/autotuner.py\", line 229, in <dictcomp>\n    timings = {config: self._bench(*args, config=config, **kwargs) for config in pruned_configs}\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/runtime/autotuner.py\", line 164, in _bench\n    return self.do_bench(kernel_call, quantiles=(0.5, 0.2, 0.8))\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/triton/testing.py\", line 96, in do_bench_cudagraph\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/cuda/__init__.py\", line 1162, in synchronize\n    return torch._C._cuda_synchronize()\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: operation not permitted when stream is capturing\nSearch for `cudaErrorStreamCaptureUnsupported' in https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__TYPES.html for more information.\nCUDA kernel errors might be asynchronously reported at some other API call, so the stacktrace below might be incorrect.\nFor debugging consider passing CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1\nCompile with `TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA` to enable device-side assertions.\n\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/triton-cuda-graph-auto-tune.py\", line 52, in <module>\n    with torch.cuda.graph(g):\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/cuda/graphs.py\", line 265, in __exit__\n    self.cuda_graph.capture_end()\n  File \"/data/zsm/perf/.venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/cuda/graphs.py\", line 126, in capture_end\n    super().capture_end()\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: operation failed due to a previous error during capture\nSearch for `cudaErrorStreamCaptureInvalidated' in https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__TYPES.html for more information.\nCUDA kernel errors might be asynchronously reported at some other API call, so the stacktrace below might be incorrect.\nFor debugging consider passing CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1\nCompile with `TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA` to enable device-side assertions.\n```\n\n### Environment details\n\nTriton: 3.6.0\nGPU: Nvidia H800","closed_at":"2026-06-15T03:23:46Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24322263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ThomasRaoux","id":24322263,"login":"ThomasRaoux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzIyMjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/received_events","repos_url":"https: