el first","created_at":"2026-06-13T12:01:11Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/10596#issuecomment-4698456896","id":4698456896,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10596","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs8AAAABGAzDQA","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/4698456896/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-06-13T12:01:11Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/4698456896","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2306281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jokeren","id":2306281,"login":"Jokeren","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDYyODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40085740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/he-yufeng","id":40085740,"login":"he-yufeng","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDg1NzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/he-yufeng","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-06-14T00:33:53Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Fixes #10596.\n\n`do_bench_cudagraph` calls `torch.cuda.synchronize()` while estimating and replaying the graph. If autotuning reaches it from inside an already-active CUDA graph capture, that synchronize call is not just unsupported; it invalidates the capture stream and the user gets a lower-level `cudaErrorStreamCaptureInvalidated` after the fact.\n\nThis keeps the existing expectation that autotuned kernels should be warmed before entering `torch.cuda.graph(...)`, but makes the failure mode explicit and non-destructive:\n\n- detect an active CUDA stream capture before creating benchmark streams/events\n- raise a clear `RuntimeError` that tells users to warm up autotuned kernels first\n- apply the same guard to the Proton CUDA-graph benchmark variant\n- cover the guard with a CPU-safe unit test using mocked CUDA capture state\n\n# New contributor declaration\n- [x] I am not making a trivial change, such as fixing a typo in a comment.\n\n- [x] I have written a PR description following these\n  [rules](https://cbea.ms/git-commit/#why-not-how).\n\n- [x] I have run `pre-commit run --from-ref upstream/main --to-ref HEAD`.\n\n- Select one of the following.\n  - [x] I have added tests.\n    - `/test` for `lit` tests\n    - `/unittest` for C++ tests\n    - `/python/test` for end-to-end tests\n  - [ ] This PR does not need a test because `FILL THIS IN`.\n\n- Select one of the following.\n  - [x] I have not added any `lit` tests.\n  - [ ] The `lit` tests I have added follow these [best practices](https://mlir.llvm.org/getting_started/TestingGuide/#filecheck-best-practices),\n    including the \"tests should be minimal\" section. (Usually running Python code\n    and using the instructions it generates is not minimal.)\n\nValidation:\n- `python -m py_compile python/triton/testing.py python/test/unit/runtime/test_testing.py`\n- `python -m ruff check python/triton/testing.py python/test/unit/runtime/test_testing.py`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `pre-commit run --from-ref upstream/main --to-ref HEAD`\n- stubbed guard smoke test that imports `python/triton/testing.py` with lightweight module stubs and verifies both cudagraph benchmark helpers reject active capture before `torch.cuda.synchronize()`\n\nI could not run `python -m pytest python/test/unit/runtime/test_testing.py -q` in this Windows checkout because the local Triton C extension is not built (`ImportError: cannot import name 'getenv' from 'triton._C.libtriton'`).\r\n","closed_at":"2026-06-16T09:34:33Z","comments":2,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10604/comments","created_at":"2026-06-14T00:33:52Z","draft":false,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10604/events","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10604","id":4657419785,"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/10604/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAWaHXs7mKGyH","number":10604,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pull_request":{"diff_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10604.diff","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10604","merged_at":null,"patch_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/10604.patch","u